          deckDescription: 'One standard 40-card Italian deck: four suits (swords, batons, cups, coins) with ten ranks each (ace through seven plus three face cards). No jokers; used for this Scopa variant where the ace captures all.',
          suitDescription: 'Four Italian suits (swords, batons, cups, coins). In Scopa, suits do not determine capturing; cards capture by matching the rank of a table card or by summing to a table card. All suits are equal for capture.',
